  <div class="sec-label"><div class="sec-label-num">1</div><div class="sec-label-text">The Role of an OT at PACE &amp; Reality of Community Practice</div><div class="sec-label-bar"></div></div>
  <div class="grid-2">
    <div class="card"><div class="card-title"><div class="card-icon">🏥</div>Part 1: What OTs at PACE Do</div><div class="card-body"><p style="margin-bottom:10px;color:var(--body);">OTs support participants to improve:</p><ul><li>Independence in daily activities</li><li>Safety within their environment</li><li>Participation in meaningful activities</li><li>Overall quality of life</li></ul><div style="margin-top:12px;"><p style="margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--body);">Achieved through:</p><ul><li>Functional assessments</li><li>Environmental &amp; home modifications</li><li>Assistive technology</li><li>Capacity building interventions</li></ul></div></div></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="card-title"><div class="card-icon">🌐</div>Part 2: Reality of Community Practice</div><div class="card-body"><p style="margin-bottom:10px;color:var(--body);">Participants rarely present with a single isolated issue. They often have:</p><ul><li>Multiple diagnoses or conditions</li><li>Environmental and social barriers</li><li>Mental health challenges</li><li>Limited or inconsistent supports</li><li>Complex family or living situations</li></ul><div class="callout teal" style="margin-top:14px;"><div class="callout-icon">💡</div><div class="callout-content">Progress is often <strong>non-linear</strong> — dependent on multiple interacting variables. Clinicians must be comfortable with complexity.</div></div></div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="sec-label"><div class="sec-label-num">2</div><div class="sec-label-text">Progress Over Perfection</div><div class="sec-label-bar"></div></div>
  <div class="grid-3">
    <div class="card" style="text-align:center;"><div style="font-size:32px;margin-bottom:8px;">🐢</div><div class="card-title" style="justify-content:center;">Small, Incremental</div><div class="card-body">Progress occurs through consistent, small improvements — not sudden leaps.</div></div>
    <div class="card" style="text-align:center;"><div style="font-size:32px;margin-bottom:8px;">🔄</div><div class="card-title" style="justify-content:center;">Layer Over Time</div><div class="card-body">Interventions are introduced, tested, and built upon — not delivered all at once.</div></div>
    <div class="card" style="text-align:center;"><div style="font-size:32px;margin-bottom:8px;">🎯</div><div class="card-title" style="justify-content:center;">Identify Priority Areas</div><div class="card-body">Break goals into manageable steps and reinforce small wins to build consistency.</div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="sec-label"><div class="sec-label-num">3</div><div class="sec-label-text">Biopsychosocial Approach</div><div class="sec-label-bar"></div></div>
  <div class="grid-2" style="align-items:start;">
    <div class="bio-diagram"><div class="bio-circles"><div class="bio-circle bio">Biological<br><span style="font-weight:400;font-size:10px;">Sleep · Fatigue · Health</span></div><div class="bio-circle psy">Psychological<br><span style="font-weight:400;font-size:10px;">Beliefs · Stress · Mood</span></div><div class="bio-circle soc">Social<br><span style="font-weight:400;font-size:10px;">Support · Environment · Context</span></div><div class="bio-center">Client<br>Experience</div></div></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="card-title"><div class="card-icon">🔬</div>Why This Model Matters</div><div class="card-body"><p style="margin-bottom:12px;">Pain and disability are not solely the result of tissue damage. They are shaped by context including beliefs, previous experiences, stress, and social support.</p><p style="margin-bottom:10px;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);">A BPS approach allows clinicians to:</p><ul><li>Understand the full context of a participant's presentation</li><li>Identify multiple contributing factors</li><li>Move beyond single-cause explanations</li><li>Tailor interventions more effectively</li></ul></div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="sec-label"><div class="sec-label-num">4</div><div class="sec-label-text">Complicated vs Complex Presentations</div><div class="sec-label-bar"></div></div>
  <div class="grid-2">
    <div class="card" style="border-top:3px solid #3B82F6;"><div class="card-title"><span style="font-size:20px;">🔧</span> Complicated</div><div class="card-body"><ul><li>Difficult but follows predictable patterns</li><li>Can be addressed with clear rules or processes</li><li>Tends to have consistent outcomes when managed correctly</li><li>Example: mechanical or procedural tasks</li></ul><div class="callout navy" style="margin-top:12px;"><div class="callout-icon">⚙️</div><div class="callout-content"><strong>Think:</strong> A task with many steps — but each step is known.</div></div></div></div>
    <div class="card" style="border-top:3px solid var(--green);"><div class="card-title"><span style="font-size:20px;">🕸️</span> Complex <span style="font-size:11px;font-weight:400;color:var(--slate);">— Most PACE Participants</span></div><div class="card-body"><ul><li>Multiple interacting variables</li><li>No single clear solution</li><li>Produces unpredictable outcomes</li><li>Requires ongoing adaptation</li></ul><div class="callout teal" style="margin-top:12px;"><div class="callout-icon">🧩</div><div class="callout-content"><strong>Shift from:</strong> "solving" problems → learning to manage, trial, and adapt over time.</div></div></div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="sec-label"><div class="sec-label-num">5</div><div class="sec-label-text">Ethical Model of Care</div><div class="sec-label-bar"></div></div>
  <div class="grid-4">
    <div class="card" style="text-align:center;border-top:3px solid #059669;"><div style="font-size:28px;margin-bottom:8px;">🛡️</div><div class="card-title" style="justify-content:center;font-size:13px;">Non-maleficence</div><div class="card-body" style="font-size:12px;">Avoid unnecessary harm. Do not reinforce beliefs that increase dependency.</div></div>
    <div class="card" style="text-align:center;border-top:3px solid #3B82F6;"><div style="font-size:28px;margin-bottom:8px;">❤️</div><div class="card-title" style="justify-content:center;font-size:13px;">Beneficence</div><div class="card-body" style="font-size:12px;">Act in the participant's best interest. Support meaningful, long-term outcomes.</div></div>
    <div class="card" style="text-align:center;border-top:3px solid #F59E0B;"><div style="font-size:28px;margin-bottom:8px;">🗳️</div><div class="card-title" style="justify-content:center;font-size:13px;">Autonomy</div><div class="card-body" style="font-size:12px;">Support participants to make their own decisions. Encourage independence, not reliance.</div></div>
    <div class="card" style="text-align:center;border-top:3px solid #8B5CF6;"><div style="font-size:28px;margin-bottom:8px;">📋</div><div class="card-title" style="justify-content:center;font-size:13px;">Informed Consent</div><div class="card-body" style="font-size:12px;">Ensure participants understand their options, timelines, and realistic expectations.</div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="sec-label"><div class="sec-label-num">6</div><div class="sec-label-text">Clinician Sustainability &amp; Self-Monitoring</div><div class="sec-label-bar"></div></div>
  <div class="grid-2" style="align-items:start;">
    <div class="monitor-card"><div class="monitor-title">📊 Monthly Sustainability Check-In (Rate 0–10)</div><div class="monitor-row"><span class="monitor-label">Workload</span><div class="monitor-track"><div class="monitor-fill" style="width:70%;"></div></div><span class="monitor-score">7</span></div><div class="monitor-row"><span class="monitor-label">Stress</span><div class="monitor-track"><div class="monitor-fill amber" style="width:55%;"></div></div><span class="monitor-score">5.5</span></div><div class="monitor-row"><span class="monitor-label">Sleep</span><div class="monitor-track"><div class="monitor-fill" style="width:80%;"></div></div><span class="monitor-score">8</span></div><div class="monitor-row"><span class="monitor-label">Diet</span><div class="monitor-track"><div class="monitor-fill" style="width:65%;"></div></div><span class="monitor-score">6.5</span></div><div class="monitor-row"><span class="monitor-label">Social</span><div class="monitor-track"><div class="monitor-fill" style="width:75%;"></div></div><span class="monitor-score">7.5</span></div><p style="font-size:11px;color:var(--slate);margin-top:14px;">Review regularly. Scores below 5 in any domain may signal early risk. Discuss in supervision.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="card-title"><div class="card-icon">⚡</div>Why Clinician Capacity Matters</div><div class="card-body"><p style="margin-bottom:10px;">High workload and fatigue may lead to:</p><ul><li>Reduced patience with complex participants</li><li>Increased reliance on quick solutions</li><li>Less effective communication</li><li>Missed key information in sessions</li></ul><div class="callout gold" style="margin-top:14px;"><div class="callout-icon">⚠️</div><div class="callout-content"><strong>Regular monitoring</strong> allows clinicians to identify early signs of burnout, adjust workload, and seek support before performance is affected.</div></div></div></div>
  </div>
<div class="sec-label"><div class="sec-label-num">7</div><div class="sec-label-text">Case-Based Discussion</div><div class="sec-label-bar"></div></div>
<div class="case-card" style="margin-bottom:24px;">
    <div class="case-header"><div class="case-badge">Case 1</div><div class="case-title">Sarah — "I Just Want My Old Life Back"</div></div>
    <div class="case-body">
      <div style="margin-bottom:12px;"><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;background:var(--green-pale);color:var(--green);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:600;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:12px;margin:2px 3px 2px 0;">Age: <span style="font-weight:400;">43</span></span><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;background:var(--green-pale);color:var(--green);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:600;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:12px;margin:2px 3px 2px 0;">Diagnosis: <span style="font-weight:400;">Spinal cord injury (MVC, 4 yrs ago)</span></span><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;background:var(--green-pale);color:var(--green);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:600;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:12px;margin:2px 3px 2px 0;">Setting: <span style="font-weight:400;">Community / NDIS</span></span><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;background:var(--green-pale);color:var(--green);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:600;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:12px;margin:2px 3px 2px 0;">Workshop Focus: <span style="font-weight:400;">Prioritisation · Clinician limits · Pacing</span></span></div>
      <p class="case-scenario">Sarah is a 43-year-old woman referred through the NDIS following a spinal cord injury sustained in a motor vehicle accident four years ago. She lives alone in a small unit and receives support worker assistance four mornings per week, though she frequently cancels shifts. Sarah previously worked as a nurse and identifies strongly with being independent and capable — since the accident she has become socially isolated, lost contact with friends, and reports significant guilt about relying on supports. She presents with chronic pain, reduced mobility, fatigue, low mood, poor sleep, and high stress from ongoing NDIS reviews. Her home has a narrow bathroom, no shower rail or seating, poor kitchen setup, and limited storage. She rarely leaves home. In her first session Sarah lists five goals simultaneously — independence, stopping support workers, returning to work, exercising, and reconnecting socially — then becomes overwhelmed when you ask where to start.</p>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:10px;margin:16px 0;"><div style="background:#FEF2F2;border:1px solid #FCA5A5;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;">
        <div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);letter-spacing:0.07em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px;">⚠️ Primary Challenges</div>
        <ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Chronic pain + fatigue + deconditioning</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Low mood and social isolation</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Home environment: no rails, unsafe shower</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Overcrowded goal list — no prioritisation</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Identity grief: "I was a nurse; I should cope"</li></ul></div><div style="background:var(--gold-pale);border:1px solid #E8C070;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;">
        <div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);letter-spacing:0.07em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px;">🎯 Participant Goals</div>
        <ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Become independent (no support workers)</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Return to nursing or similar work</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Start exercising again</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Reconnect with friends and community</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Immediate: "fix everything now"</li></ul></div><div style="background:var(--green-xpale);border:1px solid var(--green-pale);border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;">
        <div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);letter-spacing:0.07em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px;">🏢 Context Factors</div>
        <ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Lives alone — limited informal support</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">No shower rail, unsafe transfers</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Poor public transport access</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">NDIS review stress — high anxiety</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">New graduate OT: pressure to deliver quickly</li></ul></div></div>
      <div class="callout gold" style="margin:14px 0 0;"><div class="callout-icon">⚠️</div><div class="callout-content"><strong>Clinician challenge:</strong> A new graduate OT feels pressure to address all of Sarah's concerns in early sessions and leaves feeling emotionally drained. What has gone wrong, and how should this be managed?</div></div>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 280px;gap:16px;margin-top:16px;">
      <div style="background:var(--green-xpale);border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:18px 20px;">
        <div style="font-size:10.5px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--green);margin-bottom:12px;">Discussion Questions</div>
        <ol style="padding-left:18px;"><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">What are the primary drivers currently impacting Sarah's function — distinguish physical, psychological, and environmental factors.</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">Sarah has five stated goals. How would you prioritise these, and what framework would guide that decision?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">What would an appropriate first session focus on — and what would you deliberately leave for later sessions?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">What risks exist if the OT attempts to address all five goals simultaneously in early sessions?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">Which of Sarah's concerns extend beyond OT scope, and what MDT involvement would be appropriate?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">How does the concept of "progress not perfection" apply to the way you would frame goals with Sarah?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">How might Sarah's professional identity as a nurse complicate her engagement with OT support?</li></ol>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div style="background:var(--navy);border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;margin-bottom:10px;">
          <div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:8px;">Facilitator Focus</div>
          <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:2px;"><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">Prioritisation</span><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">Clinician boundaries</span><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">Therapeutic alliance</span><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">Identity complexity</span><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">Avoiding over-intervention</span></div>
        </div>
        <div style="background:var(--gold-pale);border:1px solid #E8C070;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;">
          <div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7A5010;margin-bottom:8px;">💡 Facilitator Insight</div>
          <ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">→ The correct move is NOT "do more" — it is simplify and prioritise.</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">→ Focus session 1 on rapport and understanding, not solving.</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">→ Sarah's identity as a nurse creates resistance to receiving care — this must be named gently.</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">→ NDIS stress + low mood + social isolation may warrant Psychology referral before capacity building.</li></ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    </div>
  </div><div class="case-card" style="margin-bottom:24px;">
    <div class="case-header"><div class="case-badge">Case 2</div><div class="case-title">Ethan — "Strategies That Will Finally Work"</div></div>
    <div class="case-body">
      <div style="margin-bottom:12px;"><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;background:var(--green-pale);color:var(--green);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:600;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:12px;margin:2px 3px 2px 0;">Age: <span style="font-weight:400;">8</span></span><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;background:var(--green-pale);color:var(--green);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:600;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:12px;margin:2px 3px 2px 0;">Diagnosis: <span style="font-weight:400;">ASD + ADHD</span></span><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;background:var(--green-pale);color:var(--green);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:600;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:12px;margin:2px 3px 2px 0;">Setting: <span style="font-weight:400;">Paediatric / Community</span></span><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;background:var(--green-pale);color:var(--green);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:600;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:12px;margin:2px 3px 2px 0;">Workshop Focus: <span style="font-weight:400;">Complexity · Family systems · MDT pacing</span></span></div>
      <p class="case-scenario">Ethan is an 8-year-old referred for OT support following diagnosis of Autism Spectrum Disorder and ADHD. He lives with his parents and younger sister. Ethan experiences significant emotional dysregulation, sensory sensitivities, difficulty with transitions, and poor tolerance of community environments. Morning routines have broken down and school reports are escalating with behavioural incidents. Ethan's mother reports poor sleep, increasing stress, and difficulty managing family routines — his father works long hours and is minimally involved. The family recently changed schools due to bullying. They are already engaged with psychology, speech pathology, and behavioural support. Despite this, the family frequently requests "strategies that will finally work" and appear to expect the OT to lead all care planning. The home environment has inconsistent routines, high noise levels, poor sleep schedules, and no designated regulation space.</p>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:10px;margin:16px 0;"><div style="background:#FEF2F2;border:1px solid #FCA5A5;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;">
        <div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);letter-spacing:0.07em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px;">⚠️ Primary Challenges</div>
        <ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Emotional dysregulation — multiple triggers</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Sensory sensitivities across environments</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Chaotic home routine — inconsistent structure</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Parent burnout: mum overwhelmed, dad disengaged</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Multiple services: risk of conflicting strategies</li></ul></div><div style="background:var(--gold-pale);border:1px solid #E8C070;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;">
        <div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);letter-spacing:0.07em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px;">🎯 Family Goals</div>
        <ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Improved school participation</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Fewer meltdowns at home</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Smoother morning routines</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Improved emotional regulation</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Parents want "the one thing that fixes it"</li></ul></div><div style="background:var(--green-xpale);border:1px solid var(--green-pale);border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;">
        <div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);letter-spacing:0.07em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px;">🏢 Context Factors</div>
        <ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">New school — adjustment period</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Multiple clinicians without shared plan</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Father not engaged in therapy</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">No sensory/regulation space in home</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Family expecting OT to lead all planning</li></ul></div></div>
      <div class="callout gold" style="margin:14px 0 0;"><div class="callout-icon">⚠️</div><div class="callout-content"><strong>Clinician challenge:</strong> The OT feels pressure to provide immediate solutions and reduce family distress quickly. The family also appears to expect the OT to coordinate all care. How should the OT manage this expectation?</div></div>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 280px;gap:16px;margin-top:16px;">
      <div style="background:var(--green-xpale);border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:18px 20px;">
        <div style="font-size:10.5px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--green);margin-bottom:12px;">Discussion Questions</div>
        <ol style="padding-left:18px;"><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">What factors are contributing to Ethan's difficulties — separate environmental, sensory, and behavioural contributors.</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">Which challenges are most appropriate for OT to lead, and which are better led by other disciplines?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">What should be prioritised in the first 2–3 sessions — and what should be deliberately deferred?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">What risks exist if too many strategies are introduced across too many domains simultaneously?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">How can the OT support the family without overextending scope or creating dependency on OT for all decisions?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">How would you structure MDT communication to align goals and avoid conflicting advice to the family?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">How might father disengagement affect therapy progress, and how would you approach this?</li></ol>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div style="background:var(--navy);border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;margin-bottom:10px;">
          <div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:8px;">Facilitator Focus</div>
          <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:2px;"><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">Family systems</span><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">MDT collaboration</span><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">Environmental contribution</span><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">Scope management</span><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">Realistic pacing</span></div>
        </div>
        <div style="background:var(--gold-pale);border:1px solid #E8C070;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;">
          <div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7A5010;margin-bottom:8px;">💡 Facilitator Insight</div>
          <ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">→ Complex situations require layered intervention over time — resist the urge to provide everything at once.</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">→ The family's frustration ("strategies that finally work") signals previous experiences of surface-level change — address this directly.</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">→ OT role here is environment modification + routine design — not leading all care.</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">→ A shared MDT goal-setting meeting would significantly reduce conflicting messaging to the family.</li></ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    </div>
  </div><div class="takeaways-box">
    <h3>Key Takeaways</h3>
    <div class="takeaways-grid">
      <div class="takeaway-item">Occupational therapy at PACE requires a flexible, client-centred approach</div>
      <div class="takeaway-item">A biopsychosocial approach provides a more complete picture of presentations</div>
      <div class="takeaway-item">Most participants present with complex, not complicated, challenges</div>
      <div class="takeaway-item">Ethical care underpins all clinical decision-making at PACE</div>
      <div class="takeaway-item">Progress is gradual and achieved through layered intervention over time</div>
      <div class="takeaway-item">Clinician sustainability is essential for consistent, high-quality care</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  </div>
</div>




