    <div class="timeline-seg" style="background:#FBF3E0;"><div class="ts-time" style="color:#B07820;">45-57 min</div><div class="ts-label" style="color:#7A5010;">Case-based discussion</div></div>
    <div class="timeline-seg" style="background:#E4F2EF;"><div class="ts-time" style="color:var(--green);">57-60 min</div><div class="ts-label" style="color:var(--green);">Takeaways &amp; close</div></div>
  </div>

  <div class="sec-label"><div class="sec-label-num">1</div><div class="sec-label-text">What Is Motivational Interviewing?</div><div class="sec-label-bar"></div></div>
  <div class="grid-2" style="margin-bottom:16px;">
    <div class="card"><div class="card-title"><div class="card-icon">🧭</div>Definition &amp; Origins</div><div class="card-body"><p style="margin-bottom:10px;">First developed in the <strong style="color:var(--navy);">1980s</strong> by clinical psychologists William R. Miller and Stephen Rollnick to support patients with substance use disorders. Now an established, evidence-based approach for all health professionals.</p><div class="callout teal" style="margin-top:10px;"><div class="callout-icon">💡</div><div class="callout-content">MI is a <strong>patient-centred, collaborative method</strong> for enhancing intrinsic motivation by exploring and resolving ambivalence. The practitioner does not impose change — they cultivate and support self-directed change.</div></div></div></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="card-title"><div class="card-icon">⚖️</div>MI Spirit vs Authoritative Style</div><div class="card-body"><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:10px;"><div style="background:var(--green-pale);border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:12px;"><div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:700;color:var(--green);letter-spacing:0.08em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px;">✅ MI Spirit</div><div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.6;"><div style="padding:3px 0;"><strong>Collaboration</strong> — joint decision making</div><div style="padding:3px 0;"><strong>Evocation</strong> — draw out internal motivation</div><div style="padding:3px 0;"><strong>Autonomy</strong> — it is the client's choice</div></div></div><div style="background:#FEF2F2;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:12px;"><div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:700;color:#DC2626;letter-spacing:0.08em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px;">❌ Avoid</div><div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.6;"><div style="padding:3px 0;"><strong>Confrontation</strong> — imposing insight</div><div style="padding:3px 0;"><strong>Education-as-telling</strong> — "you need to do X"</div><div style="padding:3px 0;"><strong>Authority</strong> — instructing change</div></div></div></div></div></div>
  </div>

  <div class="sec-label"><div class="sec-label-num">2</div><div class="sec-label-text">The 4 Steps of Motivational Interviewing</div><div class="sec-label-bar"></div></div>
  <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:12px;margin-bottom:8px;">
    <div class="card" style="text-align:center;padding:22px 16px;"><div style="width:44px;height:44px;background:var(--green);border-radius:50%;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#fff;margin:0 auto 12px;">1</div><div style="font-size:14px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:8px;">Engaging</div><div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--slate);line-height:1.5;">Establish a trusting relationship and develop rapport before anything else.</div></div>
    <div class="card" style="text-align:center;padding:22px 16px;"><div style="width:44px;height:44px;background:#3B82F6;border-radius:50%;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#fff;margin:0 auto 12px;">2</div><div style="font-size:14px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:8px;">Focusing</div><div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--slate);line-height:1.5;">Clarify the goal with the client. Have them name the target behaviour and potential barriers.</div></div>
    <div class="card" style="text-align:center;padding:22px 16px;"><div style="width:44px;height:44px;background:#F59E0B;border-radius:50%;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#fff;margin:0 auto 12px;">3</div><div style="font-size:14px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:8px;">Evoking</div><div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--slate);line-height:1.5;">Draw out the client's own motivation and reasons for change. Reinforce change talk.</div></div>
    <div class="card" style="text-align:center;padding:22px 16px;"><div style="width:44px;height:44px;background:#8B5CF6;border-radius:50%;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#fff;margin:0 auto 12px;">4</div><div style="font-size:14px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:8px;">Planning</div><div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--slate);line-height:1.5;">Help the client identify strategies, remove barriers, and establish tangible steps toward their goal.</div></div>
  </div>

  <div class="sec-label"><div class="sec-label-num">3</div><div class="sec-label-text">Stages of Behaviour Change — &amp; What the Clinician Does</div><div class="sec-label-bar"></div></div>
  <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:16px;">
    <div class="card-title"><div class="card-icon">🔄</div>The Transtheoretical Model — Participants Move Forwards and Backwards</div>
    <div class="stages-flow">
      <div class="stage-node"><div class="stage-circle" style="background:#94A3B8;">Pre-<br>think</div><div class="stage-label">Precontemplation</div><div class="stage-desc">Not yet considering change</div></div>
      <div class="stage-node"><div class="stage-circle" style="background:#F59E0B;">🤔</div><div class="stage-label">Contemplation</div><div class="stage-desc">Aware but unsure</div></div>
      <div class="stage-node"><div class="stage-circle" style="background:#3B82F6;">📝</div><div class="stage-label">Preparation</div><div class="stage-desc">Beginning to plan</div></div>
      <div class="stage-node"><div class="stage-circle" style="background:var(--green);">🚀</div><div class="stage-label">Action</div><div class="stage-desc">Actively making changes</div></div>
      <div class="stage-node"><div class="stage-circle" style="background:#059669;">✅</div><div class="stage-label">Maintenance</div><div class="stage-desc">Sustaining behaviours</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div style="border-radius:var(--r);overflow:hidden;border:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:16px;">
    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 1fr;background:var(--navy);"><div style="padding:10px 16px;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--gold);">Stage</div><div style="padding:10px 16px;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--gold);">Clinician's Primary Task</div><div style="padding:10px 16px;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--gold);">OT Example</div></div>
    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 1fr;background:var(--white);border-top:1px solid var(--border);"><div style="padding:12px 16px;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:600;color:#64748B;border-right:1px solid var(--border);">Precontemplation</div><div style="padding:12px 16px;font-size:12.5px;color:var(--body);border-right:1px solid var(--border);">Raise awareness. Don't push change.</div><div style="padding:12px 16px;font-size:12.5px;color:var(--slate);">Explore what a typical day looks like; plant seeds about function</div></div>
    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 1fr;background:var(--green-xpale);border-top:1px solid var(--border);"><div style="padding:12px 16px;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:600;color:#92400E;border-right:1px solid var(--border);">Contemplation</div><div style="padding:12px 16px;font-size:12.5px;color:var(--body);border-right:1px solid var(--border);">Resolve ambivalence. Help them choose change.</div><div style="padding:12px 16px;font-size:12.5px;color:var(--slate);">Explore pros/cons of current vs changed routine</div></div>
    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 1fr;background:var(--white);border-top:1px solid var(--border);"><div style="padding:12px 16px;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:600;color:#1D4ED8;border-right:1px solid var(--border);">Preparation</div><div style="padding:12px 16px;font-size:12.5px;color:var(--body);border-right:1px solid var(--border);">Help identify appropriate strategies.</div><div style="padding:12px 16px;font-size:12.5px;color:var(--slate);">Co-design a graded activity plan together</div></div>
    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 1fr;background:var(--green-xpale);border-top:1px solid var(--border);"><div style="padding:12px 16px;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:600;color:var(--green);border-right:1px solid var(--border);">Action</div><div style="padding:12px 16px;font-size:12.5px;color:var(--body);border-right:1px solid var(--border);">Support implementation. Limit relapse risk.</div><div style="padding:12px 16px;font-size:12.5px;color:var(--slate);">Review what's working; trouble-shoot barriers</div></div>
    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 1fr;background:var(--white);border-top:1px solid var(--border);"><div style="padding:12px 16px;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:600;color:#059669;border-right:1px solid var(--border);">Maintenance</div><div style="padding:12px 16px;font-size:12.5px;color:var(--body);border-right:1px solid var(--border);">Build skills for sustaining habits long term.</div><div style="padding:12px 16px;font-size:12.5px;color:var(--slate);">Reinforce identity-level change; plan for setbacks</div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="callout teal"><div class="callout-icon">💡</div><div class="callout-content">Attempting the same clinical approach across all stages leads to resistance and disengagement. <strong>Match your task to the client's stage.</strong></div></div>

  <div class="sec-label"><div class="sec-label-num">4</div><div class="sec-label-text">The Decision Line — Is the Client Ready to Act?</div><div class="sec-label-bar"></div></div>
  <div class="decision-line">
    <div class="dl-labels"><span class="dl-not-ready">← NOT READY</span><span style="color:var(--slate);font-size:11px;font-weight:500;">CLINICIAN ASSESSES READINESS</span><span class="dl-ready">READY →</span></div>
    <div class="dl-track"><div class="dl-marker" style="left:25%;color:#DC2626;background:#DC2626;"></div><div class="dl-marker" style="left:75%;color:#059669;background:#059669;"></div></div>
    <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;margin-top:6px;margin-bottom:16px;"><div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--slate);">← Build motivation &amp; confidence first</div><div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--slate);">Plan, act &amp; implement →</div></div>
    <div class="dl-zones">
      <div class="dl-zone left"><h4>❌ Not Ready for Action</h4><ul><li>Build understanding and insight</li><li>Explore concerns and fears</li><li>Support reflection and awareness</li><li>Don't push action — it creates resistance</li></ul></div>
      <div class="dl-zone right"><h4>✅ Ready for Action</h4><ul><li>Move to planning and goal setting</li><li>Implement strategies collaboratively</li><li>Build on momentum with small wins</li><li>Reinforce and review regularly</li></ul></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="sec-label"><div class="sec-label-num">5</div><div class="sec-label-text">The MI Toolkit — Conversation Tools</div><div class="sec-label-bar"></div></div>
  <div style="font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:10px;">OARS — Core Communication Skills</div>
  <div class="oars-grid" style="margin-bottom:20px;">
    <div class="oar-card"><div class="oar-header"><div class="oar-letter">O</div><div class="oar-name">Open Questions</div></div><div class="oar-body"><p class="oar-desc">Encourage exploration and reflection. Avoid yes/no questions.</p><div class="oar-example">"What would you like to be able to do more independently?"</div></div></div>
    <div class="oar-card"><div class="oar-header"><div class="oar-letter">A</div><div class="oar-name">Affirmations</div></div><div class="oar-body"><p class="oar-desc">Genuinely acknowledge the client's strengths and efforts.</p><div class="oar-example">"You've already made some important changes — that takes real commitment."</div></div></div>
    <div class="oar-card"><div class="oar-header"><div class="oar-letter">R</div><div class="oar-name">Reflective Listening</div></div><div class="oar-body"><p class="oar-desc">Demonstrate understanding and build rapport through reflection.</p><div class="oar-example">"It sounds like you want more independence, but you're worried about making things worse."</div></div></div>
    <div class="oar-card"><div class="oar-header"><div class="oar-letter">S</div><div class="oar-name">Summaries</div></div><div class="oar-body"><p class="oar-desc">Reinforce key points and ensure shared understanding.</p><div class="oar-example">"So being able to cook for yourself again is really important to you right now."</div></div></div>
  </div>
  <div style="font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:10px;">RULE — The Clinician Mindset</div>
  <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:10px;margin-bottom:20px;">
    <div style="background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--r-sm);border:1px solid var(--border);padding:14px;text-align:center;"><div style="font-size:24px;font-weight:800;color:#EF4444;margin-bottom:6px;">R</div><div style="font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:4px;">Resist</div><div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--slate);line-height:1.45;">Resist the righting reflex — the urge to fix and correct immediately</div></div>
    <div style="background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--r-sm);border:1px solid var(--border);padding:14px;text-align:center;"><div style="font-size:24px;font-weight:800;color:#F59E0B;margin-bottom:6px;">U</div><div style="font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:4px;">Understand</div><div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--slate);line-height:1.45;">Understand the client's own motivations, not what you think they should want</div></div>
    <div style="background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--r-sm);border:1px solid var(--border);padding:14px;text-align:center;"><div style="font-size:24px;font-weight:800;color:var(--green);margin-bottom:6px;">L</div><div style="font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:4px;">Listen</div><div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--slate);line-height:1.45;">Listen with empathy — seek to understand before seeking to be understood</div></div>
    <div style="background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--r-sm);border:1px solid var(--border);padding:14px;text-align:center;"><div style="font-size:24px;font-weight:800;color:#8B5CF6;margin-bottom:6px;">E</div><div style="font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:4px;">Empower</div><div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--slate);line-height:1.45;">Empower the client — support their confidence and autonomy to change</div></div>
  </div>
  <div style="font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:10px;">Change Talk — What to Listen For</div>
  <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:10px;margin-bottom:20px;">
    <div style="background:var(--green-pale);border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;border:1px solid var(--border);"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:var(--green);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.08em;margin-bottom:6px;">Disadvantages</div><div style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.5;">Explore the downsides of staying as things are now</div><div style="font-size:11.5px;color:var(--slate);margin-top:8px;font-style:italic;">"What isn't working for you at the moment?"</div></div>
    <div style="background:#FFF8EC;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;border:1px solid var(--border);"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#B07820;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.08em;margin-bottom:6px;">Advantages</div><div style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.5;">Explore what would improve if a new behaviour was adopted</div><div style="font-size:11.5px;color:var(--slate);margin-top:8px;font-style:italic;">"What would be different if you could manage that independently?"</div></div>
    <div style="background:#EFF6FF;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;border:1px solid var(--border);"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#1D4ED8;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.08em;margin-bottom:6px;">Optimism</div><div style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.5;">Build confidence that change is possible for this person</div><div style="font-size:11.5px;color:var(--slate);margin-top:8px;font-style:italic;">"What makes you think you could manage this if you tried?"</div></div>
    <div style="background:#F5F3FF;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;border:1px solid var(--border);"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#7C3AED;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.08em;margin-bottom:6px;">Intention</div><div style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.5;">Elicit statements of commitment and forward intention</div><div style="font-size:11.5px;color:var(--slate);margin-top:8px;font-style:italic;">"It sounds like you really want to give this a go — is that right?"</div></div>
  </div>

  <div class="sec-label"><div class="sec-label-num">6</div><div class="sec-label-text">Turning Motivation into Habit — 4 Laws of Behaviour Change</div><div class="sec-label-bar"></div></div>
  <div class="quadrant-grid" style="margin-bottom:16px;">
    <div class="quad-cell"><div class="quad-icon">👁️</div><div class="quad-title">Make it Obvious</div><div class="quad-desc">The cue for the behaviour must be visible and clear.</div><div style="margin-top:10px;font-size:11.5px;font-style:italic;color:var(--green);background:var(--green-pale);padding:6px 10px;border-radius:6px;">OT: Lay out equipment the night before; use visual schedules</div></div>
    <div class="quad-cell"><div class="quad-icon">🪶</div><div class="quad-title">Make it Easy</div><div class="quad-desc">Reduce friction. The behaviour should require minimal effort to start.</div><div style="margin-top:10px;font-size:11.5px;font-style:italic;color:var(--green);background:var(--green-pale);padding:6px 10px;border-radius:6px;">OT: Start with 2-minute routines; grade up gradually</div></div>
    <div class="quad-cell"><div class="quad-icon">😊</div><div class="quad-title">Make it Enjoyable</div><div class="quad-desc">Align the behaviour with the person's interests, values and preferences.</div><div style="margin-top:10px;font-size:11.5px;font-style:italic;color:var(--green);background:var(--green-pale);padding:6px 10px;border-radius:6px;">OT: Connect tasks to meaningful roles (parent, worker, carer)</div></div>
    <div class="quad-cell"><div class="quad-icon">🏆</div><div class="quad-title">Make it Satisfying</div><div class="quad-desc">Provide a sense of achievement or reward. Immediate positive feedback reinforces repetition.</div><div style="margin-top:10px;font-size:11.5px;font-style:italic;color:var(--green);background:var(--green-pale);padding:6px 10px;border-radius:6px;">OT: Celebrate small wins; track visible progress</div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="callout navy"><div class="callout-icon">📖</div><div class="callout-content">Adapted from <em>Atomic Habits</em> by James Clear. If tasks are too complex, unclear, or not meaningful — participants are unlikely to engage consistently, regardless of their stated motivation.</div></div>

  <div class="sec-label"><div class="sec-label-num">7</div><div class="sec-label-text">Resource Allocation &amp; Decision Making Tools</div><div class="sec-label-bar"></div></div>
  <div class="grid-2" style="margin-bottom:16px;">
    <div class="card"><div class="card-title"><div class="card-icon">⚖️</div>Occupational Resource Allocation</div><div class="card-body"><p style="margin-bottom:12px;font-size:13px;">Clients have limited energy and time. This tool helps them see how they currently allocate resources vs how they <em>want</em> to:</p><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:8px;margin-bottom:12px;"><div style="background:var(--green-pale);border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:12px;text-align:center;"><div style="font-size:20px;margin-bottom:4px;">🏠</div><div style="font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);">Self-Care</div><div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--slate);margin-top:4px;">ADLs, hygiene, health</div><div style="font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:var(--green);margin-top:8px;">___/10</div></div><div style="background:#FFF8EC;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:12px;text-align:center;"><div style="font-size:20px;margin-bottom:4px;">💼</div><div style="font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);">Productivity</div><div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--slate);margin-top:4px;">Work, study, roles</div><div style="font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#B07820;margin-top:8px;">___/10</div></div><div style="background:#EFF6FF;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:12px;text-align:center;"><div style="font-size:20px;margin-bottom:4px;">🎨</div><div style="font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);">Leisure</div><div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--slate);margin-top:4px;">Social, creative, fun</div><div style="font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#1D4ED8;margin-top:8px;">___/10</div></div><div style="background:#F5F3FF;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:12px;text-align:center;"><div style="font-size:20px;margin-bottom:4px;">😴</div><div style="font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);">Rest &amp; Recovery</div><div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--slate);margin-top:4px;">Sleep, downtime, recovery</div><div style="font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#7C3AED;margin-top:8px;">___/10</div></div></div><div style="font-size:11.5px;color:var(--slate);font-style:italic;">10 total points to distribute. "Where are you currently giving your points?" then "Where would you <em>like</em> to give them?"</div></div></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="card-title"><div class="card-icon">📊</div>Decision Making Matrix</div><div class="card-body"><p style="margin-bottom:12px;font-size:13px;">Explore the client's own reasoning about staying the same vs changing:</p><div style="border-radius:var(--r-sm);overflow:hidden;border:1px solid var(--border);"><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;"><div style="background:var(--border);padding:8px;text-align:center;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);border-right:1px solid var(--white);">If things stay as they are</div><div style="background:var(--border);padding:8px;text-align:center;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);">If new behaviour is adopted</div></div><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;"><div style="background:#D1FAE5;padding:10px;text-align:center;border-right:1px solid var(--border);border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);"><div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:700;color:#065F46;margin-bottom:4px;">PROS</div><div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--slate);font-style:italic;min-height:40px;">Less effort, familiar, predictable</div></div><div style="background:#D1FAE5;padding:10px;text-align:center;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);"><div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:700;color:#065F46;margin-bottom:4px;">PROS</div><div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--slate);font-style:italic;min-height:40px;">Client to identify their own…</div></div></div><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;"><div style="background:#FEE2E2;padding:10px;text-align:center;border-right:1px solid var(--border);"><div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:700;color:#991B1B;margin-bottom:4px;">CONS</div><div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--slate);font-style:italic;min-height:40px;">Client to identify their own…</div></div><div style="background:#FEE2E2;padding:10px;text-align:center;"><div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:700;color:#991B1B;margin-bottom:4px;">CONS</div><div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--slate);font-style:italic;min-height:40px;">Client to identify their own…</div></div></div></div><div class="callout teal" style="margin-top:12px;padding:10px 14px;"><div class="callout-content" style="font-size:11.5px;">The client fills this in — not the clinician. Their words carry far more weight than yours.</div></div></div></div>
  </div>

  <div class="sec-label"><div class="sec-label-num">8</div><div class="sec-label-text">Understanding &amp; Addressing Misconceptions</div><div class="sec-label-bar"></div></div>
  <div class="misconception-grid" style="margin-bottom:16px;">
    <div class="mis-card gap"><div class="mis-label">Type 1 — Missing Bits</div><div class="mis-title">🕳️ Missing Gaps</div><div class="mis-desc">Gaps in the overall coherency of knowledge. The client has a partial picture but key pieces are absent.</div><div style="margin-top:10px;padding:8px 10px;background:#EFF6FF;border-radius:6px;font-size:11.5px;font-style:italic;color:#1D4ED8;">OT example: "I should probably do something about my mobility but I'm not sure what."</div><div style="margin-top:8px;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#3B82F6;">→ Affirm what's correct. Fill gaps with targeted information nuggets.</div></div>
    <div class="mis-card grain"><div class="mis-label">Type 2 — Single Grain</div><div class="mis-title">🌾 Single Grain</div><div class="mis-desc">A simple, isolated incorrect belief — not yet sticky or connected to other beliefs.</div><div style="margin-top:10px;padding:8px 10px;background:#FFFBEB;border-radius:6px;font-size:11.5px;font-style:italic;color:#92400E;">OT example: "It's just old age — nothing can be done."</div><div style="margin-top:8px;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#F59E0B;">→ Acknowledge, offer an alternative, use MI to resolve ambivalence.</div></div>
    <div class="mis-card castle"><div class="mis-label">Type 3 — Sandcastle</div><div class="mis-title">🏰 Sandcastle</div><div class="mis-desc">A flawed mental model — grains of misconception are now clustering and reinforcing each other.</div><div style="margin-top:10px;padding:8px 10px;background:#FFF1F2;border-radius:6px;font-size:11.5px;font-style:italic;color:#9F1239;">OT example: "My condition makes any activity dangerous for me."</div><div style="margin-top:8px;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#EF4444;">→ Holistic confrontation: map the mental model visually, contrast with accurate representation.</div></div>
    <div class="mis-card stone"><div class="mis-label">Type 4 — Sandstone</div><div class="mis-title">🪨 Sandstone</div><div class="mis-desc">Deeply ingrained beliefs, tightly held and often reinforced over years by medical professionals, culture, or personal experience.</div><div style="margin-top:10px;padding:8px 10px;background:#F5F3FF;border-radius:6px;font-size:11.5px;font-style:italic;color:#4C1D95;">OT example: "Four specialists told me I'll never work again and I can see it on the MRI."</div><div style="margin-top:8px;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#8B5CF6;">→ Identify reinforcing contributors. Use MI + expectation violation.</div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="grid-2" style="margin-bottom:16px;">
    <div class="card" style="border-top:3px solid var(--gold);"><div class="card-title"><div class="card-icon">💎</div>Nuggets</div><div class="card-body"><p style="margin-bottom:10px;">Short, precise pieces of information — quick, targeted, and immediately useful.</p><div style="background:var(--gold-pale);border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:10px 14px;font-size:12.5px;"><div style="font-weight:700;color:#7A5010;margin-bottom:4px;">Best for:</div><div style="color:var(--body);">Single grain and multiple grain misconceptions.</div></div></div></div>
    <div class="card" style="border-top:3px solid #8B5CF6;"><div class="card-title"><div class="card-icon">📚</div>Novellas</div><div class="card-body"><p style="margin-bottom:10px;">Longer, richer stories (2–10 minutes) combining verbal narrative with pictures, video, or props.</p><div style="background:#F5F3FF;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:10px 14px;font-size:12.5px;"><div style="font-weight:700;color:#4C1D95;margin-bottom:4px;">Best for:</div><div style="color:var(--body);">Sandcastle-level misconceptions where a single-sentence reframe won't work.</div></div></div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="callout gold"><div class="callout-icon">⚠️</div><div class="callout-content"><strong>Key principle:</strong> Directly challenging deeply held beliefs creates resistance. Guide participants toward new understanding through conversation, reflection, and linking change to <em>their</em> goals — not yours.</div></div>

  <div class="sec-label"><div class="sec-label-num">9</div><div class="sec-label-text">Conceptual Change — Why Surface Compliance Isn't Enough</div><div class="sec-label-bar"></div></div>
  <div class="grid-2" style="margin-bottom:16px;">
    <div class="card"><div class="card-title"><div class="card-icon">🧠</div>Types of Conceptual Change</div><div class="card-body"><div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px;"><div style="padding:12px;background:#F1F5F9;border-radius:var(--r-sm);border-left:3px solid #94A3B8;"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#475569;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.08em;margin-bottom:4px;">Assimilation</div><div style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--body);">Responding using existing knowledge — fitting new information into old frameworks without changing beliefs.</div></div><div style="padding:12px;background:#FFF8EC;border-radius:var(--r-sm);border-left:3px solid var(--gold);"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#B07820;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.08em;margin-bottom:4px;">Accommodation</div><div style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--body);">Modifying existing concepts and constructing genuinely new ways of understanding the world.</div></div><div style="padding:12px;background:#FEE2E2;border-radius:var(--r-sm);border-left:3px solid #EF4444;"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#991B1B;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.08em;margin-bottom:4px;">Superficial Change</div><div style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--body);">A new belief forms but stays isolated — no influence on other thinking. Weak or no behaviour change results.</div></div><div style="padding:12px;background:var(--green-pale);border-radius:var(--r-sm);border-left:3px solid var(--green);"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:var(--green);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.08em;margin-bottom:4px;">Deep Conceptual Change ✅</div><div style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--body);">New understanding influences other beliefs — durable, transferable to new situations, and drives lasting behaviour change.</div></div></div></div></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="card-title"><div class="card-icon">🎯</div>Learning Variables — What Shapes Change</div><div class="card-body"><p style="margin-bottom:12px;font-size:13px;">Four factors determine whether conceptual change actually occurs:</p><div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;"><div style="display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:flex-start;padding:10px;background:var(--green-xpale);border-radius:var(--r-sm);"><div style="font-size:20px;flex-shrink:0;">🧑</div><div><div style="font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);">Learner</div><div style="font-size:11.5px;color:var(--slate);">The person engaging in change — their readiness, beliefs, and prior experience</div></div></div><div style="display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:flex-start;padding:10px;background:#FFF8EC;border-radius:var(--r-sm);"><div style="font-size:20px;flex-shrink:0;">🧑‍⚕️</div><div><div style="font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);">Deliverer</div><div style="font-size:11.5px;color:var(--slate);">The clinician facilitating change — their style, rapport, and therapeutic alliance</div></div></div><div style="display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:flex-start;padding:10px;background:#EFF6FF;border-radius:var(--r-sm);"><div style="font-size:20px;flex-shrink:0;">💬</div><div><div style="font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);">Message</div><div style="font-size:11.5px;color:var(--slate);">Must be <strong>comprehensible, plausible, coherent</strong>, and <strong>compelling</strong> — or it won't land</div></div></div><div style="display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:flex-start;padding:10px;background:#F5F3FF;border-radius:var(--r-sm);"><div style="font-size:20px;flex-shrink:0;">🏢</div><div><div style="font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);">Context</div><div style="font-size:11.5px;color:var(--slate);">The physical and social-psychological environment where change takes place</div></div></div></div></div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="callout teal"><div class="callout-icon">🎯</div><div class="callout-content">The goal is not compliance — it is <strong>deep conceptual change</strong> that shifts how a participant understands their situation, leading to durable and transferable behaviour change.</div></div>

  <div class="sec-label"></div>
  <div class="sec-label"><div class="sec-label-num">10</div><div class="sec-label-text">Case-Based Discussion</div><div class="sec-label-bar"></div></div><div class="case-card" style="margin-bottom:24px;">
    <div class="case-header"><div class="case-badge">Case 1</div><div class="case-title">Maria — "I Know What I Should Do… But Every Time I Try I Crash"</div></div>
    <div class="case-body">
      <div style="margin-bottom:12px;"><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;background:var(--green-pale);color:var(--green);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:600;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:12px;margin:2px 3px 2px 0;">Age: <span style="font-weight:400;">39</span></span><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;background:var(--green-pale);color:var(--green);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:600;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:12px;margin:2px 3px 2px 0;">Presentation: <span style="font-weight:400;">Chronic pain + fatigue</span></span><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;background:var(--green-pale);color:var(--green);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:600;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:12px;margin:2px 3px 2px 0;">Workshop Focus: <span style="font-weight:400;">Ambivalence · Fear-based avoidance · MI</span></span></div>
      <p class="case-scenario">Maria is a 39-year-old woman with chronic pain and fatigue following a workplace injury. She avoids most activity and frequently says "I know I should do more, but every time I try I crash." She has seen multiple clinicians and reports "nothing has worked." She fears flare-ups intensely, consistently avoids implementing strategies, and frequently cancels appointments.</p>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:10px;margin:16px 0;"><div style="background:#FEF2F2;border:1px solid #FCA5A5;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);letter-spacing:0.07em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px;">⚠️ Key Barriers</div><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Intense fear of flare-up — avoidance cycle</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">"Nothing has worked" = sandstone belief forming</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Appointments frequently cancelled</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Ambivalence: wants change, fears the attempt</li></ul></div><div style="background:#EFF6FF;border:1px solid #BFCBFE;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);letter-spacing:0.07em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px;">🔄 Stage Indicators</div><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Contemplation — knows she should change</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Confidence low (fear dominant)</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Not ready to commit to new strategies</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Fear is the primary barrier, not knowledge</li></ul></div><div style="background:var(--gold-pale);border:1px solid #E8C070;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);letter-spacing:0.07em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px;">🎯 Goals</div><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">More independence at home</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Social connection</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Energy to leave the house</li></ul></div></div>
      
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 280px;gap:16px;margin-top:16px;">
      <div style="background:var(--green-xpale);border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:18px 20px;">
        <div style="font-size:10.5px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--green);margin-bottom:12px;">Discussion Questions</div>
        <ol style="padding-left:18px;"><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">What stage of behaviour change is Maria in — and what is your primary clinical task?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">What type of misconception does Maria hold about activity and pain?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">What role does fear play in maintaining her avoidance cycle?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">What would be an inappropriate communication approach, and why?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">Using OARS, write two open questions and one affirmation for Maria.</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">What change talk points could you explore?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">How would you use scaling questions to guide your approach?</li></ol>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div style="background:var(--navy);border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;margin-bottom:10px;">
          <div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:8px;">Facilitator Focus</div>
          <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:2px;"><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">Fear-based avoidance</span><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">Ambivalence</span><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">MI readiness</span><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">Change talk</span></div>
        </div>
        <div style="background:var(--gold-pale);border:1px solid #E8C070;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;">
          <div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7A5010;margin-bottom:8px;">💡 Facilitator Insight</div>
          <ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">→ This is NOT a motivation problem — it is a fear and readiness problem. Don't push action.</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">→ Maria's "nothing has worked" belief is sandstone — it needs MI + gradual expectation violation.</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">→ Resist the righting reflex strongly here.</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">→ Scaling confidence first — if below 5, planning is premature.</li></ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    </div>
  </div><div class="case-card" style="margin-bottom:24px;">
    <div class="case-header"><div class="case-badge">Case 2</div><div class="case-title">David — "Agrees With Everything, Does Nothing"</div></div>
    <div class="case-body">
      <div style="margin-bottom:12px;"><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;background:var(--green-pale);color:var(--green);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:600;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:12px;margin:2px 3px 2px 0;">Age: <span style="font-weight:400;">67</span></span><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;background:var(--green-pale);color:var(--green);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:600;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:12px;margin:2px 3px 2px 0;">Presentation: <span style="font-weight:400;">Post-stroke, reduced mobility</span></span><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;background:var(--green-pale);color:var(--green);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:600;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:12px;margin:2px 3px 2px 0;">Workshop Focus: <span style="font-weight:400;">Superficial agreement · Identity · Autonomy</span></span></div>
      <p class="case-scenario">David is a 67-year-old man six months post-stroke with reduced mobility, poor balance, and difficulty showering safely. OT recommendations include grab rails and shower modifications. David agrees readily with all recommendations but consistently fails to follow through. His wife frequently answers questions on his behalf. He strongly values independence and dislikes feeling "old or disabled." He avoids discussing falls, fears about decline, or the emotional impact of the stroke.</p>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:10px;margin:16px 0;"><div style="background:#FEF2F2;border:1px solid #FCA5A5;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);letter-spacing:0.07em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px;">⚠️ Key Barriers</div><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Identity threat: modifications signal disability</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Passive agreement ≠ genuine readiness</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Wife's involvement may be undermining autonomy</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Grief about stroke — unprocessed</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Three sessions with no change = wrong approach</li></ul></div><div style="background:#EFF6FF;border:1px solid #BFCBFE;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);letter-spacing:0.07em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px;">🔄 Stage Indicators</div><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Precontemplation for home modifications</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Superficial agreement — avoiding the real conversation</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">His wife's readiness ≠ David's readiness</li></ul></div><div style="background:var(--gold-pale);border:1px solid #E8C070;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);letter-spacing:0.07em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px;">🎯 Clinical Challenge</div><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Explore identity and grief first</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Honour autonomy while addressing safety</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Re-engage David directly — wife should step back</li></ul></div></div>
      
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 280px;gap:16px;margin-top:16px;">
      <div style="background:var(--green-xpale);border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:18px 20px;">
        <div style="font-size:10.5px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--green);margin-bottom:12px;">Discussion Questions</div>
        <ol style="padding-left:18px;"><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">Is David genuinely ready to change — or is his agreement compliance to avoid the real conversation?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">What stage of behaviour change is David in for the home modifications?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">How might identity loss and grief about the stroke be influencing his engagement?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">How could the OT explore ambivalence more effectively — what OARS tools would be most useful?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">What is the impact of his wife answering for him, and how would you address this?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">What does autonomy mean in David's context?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">After three sessions without progress, what should the OT reflect on?</li></ol>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div style="background:var(--navy);border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;margin-bottom:10px;">
          <div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:8px;">Facilitator Focus</div>
          <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:2px;"><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">Superficial agreement vs readiness</span><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">Identity and grief</span><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">MI and autonomy</span><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">Family dynamics</span><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">Self-reflection</span></div>
        </div>
        <div style="background:var(--gold-pale);border:1px solid #E8C070;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;">
          <div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7A5010;margin-bottom:8px;">💡 Facilitator Insight</div>
          <ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">→ Superficial agreement is a warning sign — explore what's underneath it.</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">→ David's identity as an independent man is the primary barrier.</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">→ Ask David directly: "What would it mean for you if the rails were installed?" — then listen.</li></ul>
        </div>
