  <div class="sec-label"><div class="sec-label-num">1</div><div class="sec-label-text">Why Sustainability Matters in Clinical Practice</div><div class="sec-label-bar"></div></div>
  <div class="grid-2">
    <div class="card"><div class="card-title"><div class="card-icon">⚠️</div>When Clinicians Are Overwhelmed</div><div class="card-body"><p style="margin-bottom:10px;">Clinicians who are fatigued or overwhelmed are more likely to:</p><ul><li>Miss key information in sessions</li><li>Over- or under-prescribe interventions</li><li>Avoid difficult conversations</li><li>Experience reduced confidence in decisions</li></ul></div></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="card-title"><div class="card-icon">🌱</div>Sustainability Is a Clinical Skill</div><div class="card-body"><p style="margin-bottom:10px;">Sustainability is not just about wellbeing — it is about maintaining <strong>consistent, high-quality clinical performance over time.</strong></p><div class="callout teal"><div class="callout-icon">💡</div><div class="callout-content">Maintaining clinician sustainability directly supports better participant outcomes — not just better clinician wellbeing.</div></div></div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="sec-label"><div class="sec-label-num">2</div><div class="sec-label-text">Understanding Burnout — The Progression</div><div class="sec-label-bar"></div></div>
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-title"><div class="card-icon">📉</div>Burnout Develops Gradually — Catch It Early</div>
    <div class="burnout-bar"><div class="burnout-markers"><div class="burnout-zone">Thriving</div><div class="burnout-zone">Managing</div><div class="burnout-zone">Stressed</div><div class="burnout-zone">Fatigued</div><div class="burnout-zone">Burnout</div></div></div>
    <div class="burnout-labels"><span style="color:#059669;">Thriving</span><span style="color:#10B981;">Managing</span><span style="color:#F59E0B;">Stressed</span><span style="color:#EF4444;">Fatigued</span><span style="color:#DC2626;">Burnout</span></div>
    <div class="grid-3" style="margin-top:20px;"><div class="callout teal"><div class="callout-icon">😴</div><div class="callout-content"><strong>Physical:</strong> Fatigue, sleep issues, frequent illness, low energy</div></div><div class="callout gold"><div class="callout-icon">🧠</div><div class="callout-content"><strong>Psychological:</strong> Reduced motivation, difficulty concentrating, cynicism</div></div><div class="callout navy"><div class="callout-icon">🔌</div><div class="callout-content"><strong>Behavioural:</strong> Withdrawing, overworking, increased errors, reduced empathy</div></div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="sec-label"><div class="sec-label-num">3</div><div class="sec-label-text">A Biopsychosocial View of Clinician Health</div><div class="sec-label-bar"></div></div>
  <div class="grid-2" style="align-items:start;">
    <div class="bio-diagram"><div class="bio-circles"><div class="bio-circle bio">Biological<br><span style="font-weight:400;font-size:10px;">Sleep · Fatigue · Physical Health</span></div><div class="bio-circle psy">Psychological<br><span style="font-weight:400;font-size:10px;">Stress · Emotional Load · Cognitive Fatigue</span></div><div class="bio-circle soc">Social<br><span style="font-weight:400;font-size:10px;">Workload · Support Systems · Workplace</span></div><div class="bio-center">Clinician Performance</div></div></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="card-title"><div class="card-icon">🔗</div>How These Domains Interact</div><div class="card-body"><p style="margin-bottom:12px;">Just as we understand participants through a biopsychosocial lens, clinician wellbeing can be considered across the same three domains.</p><ul><li><strong>Biological:</strong> Sleep quality, fatigue levels, physical health and recovery</li><li><strong>Psychological:</strong> Stress, emotional load from complex cases, decision fatigue</li><li><strong>Social:</strong> Caseload demands, support from peers and supervisors, workplace culture</li></ul><div class="callout teal" style="margin-top:12px;"><div class="callout-icon">💡</div><div class="callout-content">Understanding these <strong>interacting factors</strong> allows clinicians to identify where changes are needed and address them proactively.</div></div></div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="sec-label"><div class="sec-label-num">4</div><div class="sec-label-text">Monitoring Clinical Sustainability</div><div class="sec-label-bar"></div></div>
  <div class="grid-2" style="align-items:start;">
    <div class="monitor-card"><div class="monitor-title">📊 Monthly Sustainability Dashboard (0–10)</div><div class="monitor-row"><span class="monitor-label">Workload</span><div class="monitor-track"><div class="monitor-fill red" style="width:85%;"></div></div><span class="monitor-score">8.5</span></div><div class="monitor-row"><span class="monitor-label">Stress</span><div class="monitor-track"><div class="monitor-fill amber" style="width:70%;"></div></div><span class="monitor-score">7</span></div><div class="monitor-row"><span class="monitor-label">Sleep</span><div class="monitor-track"><div class="monitor-fill amber" style="width:50%;"></div></div><span class="monitor-score">5</span></div><div class="monitor-row"><span class="monitor-label">Diet</span><div class="monitor-track"><div class="monitor-fill" style="width:65%;"></div></div><span class="monitor-score">6.5</span></div><div class="monitor-row"><span class="monitor-label">Social</span><div class="monitor-track"><div class="monitor-fill amber" style="width:40%;"></div></div><span class="monitor-score">4</span></div><p style="font-size:11px;color:#DC2626;margin-top:14px;font-weight:500;">⚠️ This example shows early warning signs.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="card-title"><div class="card-icon">🎯</div>How to Use This Tool</div><div class="card-body"><ul><li>Rate each domain honestly on a 0–10 scale</li><li>Review at least monthly, or after difficult periods</li><li>Look for patterns and downward trends</li><li>Discuss in supervision when scores drop below 5</li><li>Act on early warning signs — don't wait for crisis</li></ul><div class="callout gold" style="margin-top:14px;"><div class="callout-icon">📅</div><div class="callout-content"><strong>Regular monitoring</strong> supports early identification of risk, targeted adjustments, and ongoing self-awareness.</div></div></div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="sec-label"><div class="sec-label-num">5</div><div class="sec-label-text">Managing Workload, Emotional Load &amp; Boundaries</div><div class="sec-label-bar"></div></div>
  <div class="grid-3">
    <div class="card"><div class="card-title"><div class="card-icon">📋</div>Workload Management</div><div class="card-body"><ul><li>Focus on high-impact tasks first</li><li>Break complex tasks into manageable steps</li><li>Schedule dedicated documentation time</li><li>Allow buffer time between sessions</li><li>Balance efficiency with quality of care</li></ul></div></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="card-title"><div class="card-icon">💛</div>Managing Emotional Load</div><div class="card-body"><ul><li>Recognise emotional responses as they arise</li><li>Reflect on experiences — use supervision</li><li>Seek support before load becomes unmanageable</li><li>Maintain professional boundaries consistently</li></ul><div class="callout gold" style="margin-top:10px;padding:10px 14px;"><div class="callout-content" style="font-size:12px;">Ignoring emotional load over time is a primary driver of burnout.</div></div></div></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="card-title"><div class="card-icon">🔒</div>Setting Boundaries</div><div class="card-body"><ul><li>Define realistic session goals upfront</li><li>Avoid over-commitment with participants</li><li>Maintain appropriate communication limits</li><li>Recognise when to refer or seek support</li></ul><div class="callout teal" style="margin-top:10px;padding:10px 14px;"><div class="callout-content" style="font-size:12px;">Boundaries protect both clinician wellbeing AND the quality of care delivered.</div></div></div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="sec-label"><div class="sec-label-num">6</div><div class="sec-label-text">Case-Based Discussion</div><div class="sec-label-bar"></div></div>
  <div class="case-card" style="margin-bottom:24px;">
    <div class="case-header"><div class="case-badge">Case 1</div><div class="case-title">James — "I Don't Want to Let Anyone Down"</div></div>
    <div class="case-body">
      <div style="margin-bottom:12px;"><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;background:var(--green-pale);color:var(--green);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:600;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:12px;margin:2px 3px 2px 0;">Role: <span style="font-weight:400;">Early-career OT, community disability</span></span><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;background:var(--green-pale);color:var(--green);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:600;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:12px;margin:2px 3px 2px 0;">Workshop Focus: <span style="font-weight:400;">Burnout · Emotional load · Clinician identity</span></span></div>
      <p class="case-scenario">James is an early-career OT who has been working in community disability for eight months. He works late regularly, completes reports after hours, checks emails at night, and struggles to switch off mentally. He feels pressure to prove himself, guilt when participants aren't progressing, and anxiety about making mistakes. He frequently says "I don't want to let anyone down." He manages several participants with trauma histories and complex behavioural presentations. He believes his current level of engagement is "just part of the job."</p>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:10px;margin:16px 0;"><div style="background:#FEF2F2;border:1px solid #FCA5A5;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);letter-spacing:0.07em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px;">⚠️ Burnout Indicators</div><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Works and checks emails after hours</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Replays sessions mentally at home</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Guilt when participants are not progressing</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Anxiety about clinical decisions</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Normalising unhealthy load: "this is just the job"</li></ul></div><div style="background:#EFF6FF;border:1px solid #BFCBFE;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);letter-spacing:0.07em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px;">📊 Sustainability Domains Affected</div><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Psychological: stress, guilt, anxiety high</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Behavioural: poor boundaries, no switch-off</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Cognitive: replaying sessions, decision doubt</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Social: likely withdrawing from peers</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Belief system: perfectionism + responsibility overload</li></ul></div><div style="background:var(--gold-pale);border:1px solid #E8C070;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);letter-spacing:0.07em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px;">🧠 Driving Beliefs</div><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">"I must not let participants down"</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">"If I stop working I'm being lazy"</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">"Asking for help means I'm not capable"</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">"The harder I work the better the outcomes"</li></ul></div></div>
      <div class="callout gold" style="margin:14px 0 0;"><div class="callout-icon">⚠️</div><div class="callout-content"><strong>Clinician challenge:</strong> James tells you he is fine. What would your response be, and how would you open a genuine conversation about his sustainability?</div></div>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 280px;gap:16px;margin-top:16px;">
      <div style="background:var(--green-xpale);border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:18px 20px;">
        <div style="font-size:10.5px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--green);margin-bottom:12px;">Discussion Questions</div>
        <ol style="padding-left:18px;"><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">What early signs of burnout are visible in James — classify them across physical, psychological, and behavioural domains.</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">Which of James's beliefs are driving his unsustainable behaviour, and where might these beliefs originate?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">Which domains of the sustainability framework are most significantly affected?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">How might James's current state be impacting his clinical reasoning and the quality of his sessions?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">What specific boundaries or systems could James implement?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">How would you use the sustainability monitoring dashboard to start a conversation with James?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">What would you say to James if he said "I'm fine — this is just how the job is"?</li></ol>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div style="background:var(--navy);border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;margin-bottom:10px;">
          <div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:8px;">Facilitator Focus</div>
          <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:2px;"><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">Emotional load</span><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">Perfectionism</span><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">Clinician identity</span><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">Sustainability systems</span><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">Supervision use</span></div>
        </div>
        <div style="background:var(--gold-pale);border:1px solid #E8C070;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;">
          <div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7A5010;margin-bottom:8px;">💡 Facilitator Insight</div>
          <ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">→ James is at risk of compassion fatigue, not just tiredness — this distinction matters clinically.</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">→ His belief system is the root driver — addressing behaviours alone won't be enough.</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">→ Use the sustainability dashboard as a non-threatening entry point to the conversation.</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">→ Normalise: high emotional investment is a strength — unmanaged, it becomes a liability.</li></ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    </div>
  </div><div class="case-card" style="margin-bottom:24px;">
    <div class="case-header"><div class="case-badge">Case 2</div><div class="case-title">Sophie — "The Impossible Week"</div></div>
    <div class="case-body">
      <div style="margin-bottom:12px;"><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;background:var(--green-pale);color:var(--green);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:600;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:12px;margin:2px 3px 2px 0;">Role: <span style="font-weight:400;">Experienced OT, community caseload</span></span><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;background:var(--green-pale);color:var(--green);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:600;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:12px;margin:2px 3px 2px 0;">Workshop Focus: <span style="font-weight:400;">Workload design · Capacity vs demand</span></span></div>
      <p class="case-scenario">Sophie is an OT managing a geographically spread caseload. Her week includes long travel times, multiple reports due simultaneously, back-to-back home visits, and several emotionally demanding participants. She regularly skips lunch and uses documentation time to squeeze in extra visits. Cancellations cause further disruption. Sophie is increasingly reactive and reports feeling "constantly behind." She has noticed she is less present in sessions and making small documentation errors. She describes the situation as temporary but it has been ongoing for four months.</p>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:10px;margin:16px 0;"><div style="background:#FEF2F2;border:1px solid #FCA5A5;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);letter-spacing:0.07em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px;">⚠️ Workload Issues</div><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">No buffer time between complex visits</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Documentation displaced by extra appointments</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Travel time not accounted for in scheduling</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Reactive scheduling after cancellations</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Sustained 4 months — now a pattern</li></ul></div><div style="background:#EFF6FF;border:1px solid #BFCBFE;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);letter-spacing:0.07em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px;">📊 Performance Impact</div><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Less present during sessions</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Small documentation errors increasing</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Decision fatigue from back-to-back complexity</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Physical: skipping meals, fatigue accumulating</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Risk of clinical incident if pattern continues</li></ul></div><div style="background:var(--gold-pale);border:1px solid #E8C070;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);letter-spacing:0.07em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px;">🎯 What Needs to Change</div><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Protected documentation time — non-negotiable</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Travel time built into scheduling</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Maximum consecutive complex visits per day</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Clear cancellation protocol — don't fill reflexively</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Weekly capacity vs demand review</li></ul></div></div>
      <div class="callout gold" style="margin:14px 0 0;"><div class="callout-icon">⚠️</div><div class="callout-content"><strong>Clinician challenge:</strong> Sophie says "it's always like this at this time of year." How would you help her recognise that this is now a structural pattern?</div></div>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 280px;gap:16px;margin-top:16px;">
      <div style="background:var(--green-xpale);border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:18px 20px;">
        <div style="font-size:10.5px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--green);margin-bottom:12px;">Discussion Questions</div>
        <ol style="padding-left:18px;"><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">What workload management issues are present in Sophie's situation?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">How is Sophie's current work pattern affecting her clinical performance?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">What structural changes to her schedule would most significantly reduce pressure?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">What risks exist clinically if this pattern continues for another four months?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">How could Sophie use the sustainability framework to design a more sustainable week?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">What is the difference between a temporary busy period and a structural workload problem?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">How would you approach a conversation with Sophie's manager about this situation?</li></ol>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div style="background:var(--navy);border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;margin-bottom:10px;">
          <div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:8px;">Facilitator Focus</div>
          <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:2px;"><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">Workflow design</span><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">Capacity vs demand</span><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">Sustainable scheduling</span><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">Clinical risk</span></div>
        </div>
        <div style="background:var(--gold-pale);border:1px solid #E8C070;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;">
          <div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7A5010;margin-bottom:8px;">💡 Facilitator Insight</div>
          <ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">→ Sophie's situation is structural, not personal — the solution requires system change, not just resilience.</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">→ Documentation errors are a clinical safety flag — this should be named clearly.</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">→ Protected time for documentation is not optional — it is a clinical reasoning tool.</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">→ The "fill every cancellation" reflex is a common trap in community OT.</li></ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    </div>
  </div><div class="takeaways-box"><h3>Key Takeaways</h3><div class="takeaways-grid"><div class="takeaway-item">Sustainability is essential for maintaining high-quality clinical performance</div><div class="takeaway-item">A biopsychosocial approach applies equally to clinician wellbeing</div><div class="takeaway-item">Burnout develops gradually — identify and act on early signs</div><div class="takeaway-item">Clear boundaries support both clinician wellbeing and participant outcomes</div><div class="takeaway-item">Structured monitoring helps identify and address issues proactively</div><div class="takeaway-item">Sustainability underpins effective reasoning, behaviour change, and planning</div></div></div>
  </div>
</div>

