  <div class="sec-label"><div class="sec-label-num">1</div><div class="sec-label-text">The PEO Model</div><div class="sec-label-bar"></div></div>
  <div class="peo-diagram" style="margin-bottom:16px;">
    <div class="peo-card person"><div class="peo-letter">P</div><div class="peo-name">Person</div><ul class="peo-items"><li>Physical abilities</li><li>Cognitive capacity</li><li>Emotional factors</li><li>Health conditions</li></ul></div>
    <div class="peo-card env"><div class="peo-letter">E</div><div class="peo-name">Environment</div><ul class="peo-items"><li>Physical environment</li><li>Social supports</li><li>Accessibility</li><li>Cultural context</li></ul></div>
    <div class="peo-card occ"><div class="peo-letter">O</div><div class="peo-name">Occupation</div><ul class="peo-items"><li>Meaningful activities</li><li>Daily tasks</li><li>Roles and routines</li></ul></div>
  </div>
  <div class="callout teal"><div class="callout-icon">🎯</div><div class="callout-content"><strong>Clinical reasoning involves identifying where the mismatch is occurring</strong> — between the person, their environment, and the occupation. This guides intervention selection.</div></div>
  <div class="sec-label"><div class="sec-label-num">2</div><div class="sec-label-text">Identifying Key Drivers — The Driver Hierarchy</div><div class="sec-label-bar"></div></div>
  <div class="grid-2" style="align-items:start;">
    <div class="card"><div class="driver-pyramid"><div class="pyramid-row primary">🎯 PRIMARY DRIVER <span class="pyramid-label">— Main factor limiting performance</span></div><div class="wb-connector"></div><div class="pyramid-row secondary">🔶 SECONDARY DRIVERS <span class="pyramid-label">— Contributing factors</span></div><div class="wb-connector"></div><div class="pyramid-row background">⬜ BACKGROUND FACTORS <span class="pyramid-label">— Relevant but not immediately actionable</span></div></div></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="card-title"><div class="card-icon">🍳</div>Example: Difficulty Preparing Meals</div><div class="card-body"><p style="margin-bottom:12px;">Multiple contributing factors may be present:</p><ul><li>Reduced grip strength</li><li>Fatigue limiting standing tolerance</li><li>Poor kitchen setup and equipment</li><li>Low confidence and fear of failure</li></ul><div class="callout gold" style="margin-top:12px;"><div class="callout-icon">❓</div><div class="callout-content"><strong>Key question:</strong> "Which of these is the main factor limiting performance right now?" Identify the primary driver first.</div></div></div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="sec-label"><div class="sec-label-num">3</div><div class="sec-label-text">The Clinical Reasoning Loop</div><div class="sec-label-bar"></div></div>
  <div class="card">
    <div class="reasoning-loop"><div class="loop-node"><div class="loop-circle" style="background:var(--green);">Assess</div></div><div class="loop-arrow">→</div><div class="loop-node"><div class="loop-circle" style="background:#3B82F6;">Interpret</div></div><div class="loop-arrow">→</div><div class="loop-node"><div class="loop-circle" style="background:#F59E0B;">Act</div></div><div class="loop-arrow">→</div><div class="loop-node"><div class="loop-circle" style="background:#8B5CF6;">Review</div></div><div class="loop-arrow" style="font-size:18px;color:var(--sage);">↩</div></div>
    <div class="grid-4" style="margin-top:16px;gap:12px;"><div style="text-align:center;padding:10px;background:var(--green-xpale);border-radius:8px;"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:var(--green);">ASSESS</div><div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--slate);">Gather information. Use PEO to explore all domains.</div></div><div style="text-align:center;padding:10px;background:#EFF6FF;border-radius:8px;"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#3B82F6;">INTERPRET</div><div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--slate);">Identify primary driver. Link factors to function.</div></div><div style="text-align:center;padding:10px;background:#FFFBEB;border-radius:8px;"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#D97706;">ACT</div><div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--slate);">Intervene, trial, or refer. Target the primary driver.</div></div><div style="text-align:center;padding:10px;background:#F5F3FF;border-radius:8px;"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#7C3AED;">REVIEW</div><div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--slate);">Evaluate outcomes. Adjust approach as needed.</div></div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="sec-label"><div class="sec-label-num">4</div><div class="sec-label-text">Decision Tree — Act, Trial, or Refer?</div><div class="sec-label-bar"></div></div>
  <div class="decision-tree">
    <div class="dt-center"><div class="dt-node problem">Problem Identified via Clinical Reasoning</div></div>
    <div class="dt-arrows"><div class="dt-branch"><div class="dt-q">Strong evidence of benefit + clear clinical need + safety concern</div><div class="dt-action act">✅ Act — Intervene Directly</div></div><div class="dt-branch"><div class="dt-q">Participant unsure + multiple options + benefit unclear + high cost</div><div class="dt-action trial">🔬 Trial — Test the Approach First</div></div><div class="dt-branch"><div class="dt-q">Outside OT scope + specialist expertise needed + safety risk without input</div><div class="dt-action refer">↗ Refer — Involve Another Discipline</div></div></div>
    <div class="callout teal" style="margin-top:16px;"><div class="callout-icon">💡</div><div class="callout-content"><strong>Also consider:</strong> Is the participant ready to engage with this intervention? What stage of change are they in? This links directly to Workshop 2.</div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="sec-label"><div class="sec-label-num">5</div><div class="sec-label-text">Case-Based Discussion</div><div class="sec-label-bar"></div></div>
  <div class="case-card" style="margin-bottom:24px;">
    <div class="case-header"><div class="case-badge">Case 1</div><div class="case-title">Helen — "Too Many Problems, Not Enough Time"</div></div>
    <div class="case-body">
      <div style="margin-bottom:12px;"><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;background:var(--green-pale);color:var(--green);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:600;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:12px;margin:2px 3px 2px 0;">Age: <span style="font-weight:400;">71</span></span><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;background:var(--green-pale);color:var(--green);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:600;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:12px;margin:2px 3px 2px 0;">Diagnosis: <span style="font-weight:400;">Arthritis · Chronic pain · Falls history · Anxiety</span></span><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;background:var(--green-pale);color:var(--green);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:600;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:12px;margin:2px 3px 2px 0;">Workshop Focus: <span style="font-weight:400;">Prioritisation · Driver identification</span></span></div>
      <p class="case-scenario">Helen is a 71-year-old woman referred following two recent falls at home. She presents with arthritis, chronic pain, a falls history, and significant health anxiety. She struggles with showering, cooking, navigating stairs, and leaving home. She is deeply fearful of losing independence and moving into aged care. Her daughter frequently pushes for "quick solutions." Helen catastrophises pain, avoids activity, and has very low confidence. Her home has narrow hallways, poor lighting, no rails, and a steep entry.</p>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:10px;margin:16px 0;"><div style="background:#FEF2F2;border:1px solid #FCA5A5;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);letter-spacing:0.07em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px;">⚠️ Primary vs Secondary Drivers</div><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Primary: environmental hazards (no rails, lighting, steep entry)</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Primary: fear and avoidance amplifying functional limitation</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Secondary: deconditioning from prolonged inactivity</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Secondary: pain catastrophising limiting engagement</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Background: daughter pressure creating session disruption</li></ul></div><div style="background:#EFF6FF;border:1px solid #BFCBFE;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);letter-spacing:0.07em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px;">🧠 Reasoning Complexity</div><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">PEO mismatch: environment + psychological factors dominant</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Falls risk requires immediate environmental action</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">But environmental fixes alone won't address fear/avoidance</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Psychological factors may limit AT/HM effectiveness</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Daughter's urgency ≠ correct clinical priority</li></ul></div><div style="background:var(--gold-pale);border:1px solid #E8C070;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);letter-spacing:0.07em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px;">🎯 Intervention Considerations</div><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Home modifications: high priority for safety</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">MI needed before capacity building</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Falls confidence (FES-I) assessment valuable</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Psychology referral for catastrophising?</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Education on pain and activity — avoid reinforcing fear</li></ul></div></div>
      <div class="callout gold" style="margin:14px 0 0;"><div class="callout-icon">⚠️</div><div class="callout-content"><strong>Clinician challenge:</strong> The daughter calls after the first session and says "why aren't you just putting the rails in?" How would you respond?</div></div>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 280px;gap:16px;margin-top:16px;">
      <div style="background:var(--green-xpale);border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:18px 20px;">
        <div style="font-size:10.5px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--green);margin-bottom:12px;">Discussion Questions</div>
        <ol style="padding-left:18px;"><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">Using the PEO model, identify the key mismatches contributing to Helen's functional difficulties.</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">What are the primary drivers versus secondary contributors — and how does this change what you address first?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">Which interventions should be prioritised immediately, and which should be deferred?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">How should the OT manage the daughter's pressure for quick solutions?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">What risk exists if the OT focuses on equipment without addressing fear and avoidance?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">Would you refer to psychology — and if so, at what point and for what reason?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">How would you use the reasoning loop to structure your approach over four sessions?</li></ol>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div style="background:var(--navy);border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;margin-bottom:10px;">
          <div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:8px;">Facilitator Focus</div>
          <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:2px;"><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">Driver identification</span><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">PEO analysis</span><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">Prioritisation</span><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">MDT referral</span><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">Managing family dynamics</span></div>
        </div>
        <div style="background:var(--gold-pale);border:1px solid #E8C070;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;">
          <div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7A5010;margin-bottom:8px;">💡 Facilitator Insight</div>
          <ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">→ Home modifications are necessary but insufficient — fear is driving limitation as much as the environment.</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">→ Catastrophising and avoidance often reduce the effectiveness of environmental interventions — address them together.</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">→ Helen's fear of aged care is a powerful motivator — connect all interventions to staying home independently.</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">→ The daughter needs a clear explanation of the clinical reasoning.</li></ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    </div>
  </div><div class="case-card" style="margin-bottom:24px;">
    <div class="case-header"><div class="case-badge">Case 2</div><div class="case-title">Liam — "The Wrong Intervention?"</div></div>
    <div class="case-body">
      <div style="margin-bottom:12px;"><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;background:var(--green-pale);color:var(--green);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:600;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:12px;margin:2px 3px 2px 0;">Age: <span style="font-weight:400;">32</span></span><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;background:var(--green-pale);color:var(--green);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:600;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:12px;margin:2px 3px 2px 0;">Diagnosis: <span style="font-weight:400;">Cerebral palsy</span></span><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;background:var(--green-pale);color:var(--green);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:600;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:12px;margin:2px 3px 2px 0;">Workshop Focus: <span style="font-weight:400;">Over-prescription · True driver identification</span></span></div>
      <p class="case-scenario">Liam is a 32-year-old man with cerebral palsy. He presents with fatigue, poor endurance, and increasing difficulty with meal preparation. Previous clinicians have recommended and installed extensive equipment and home modifications. Despite this, Liam's difficulties persist. On assessment, his physical capacity has declined significantly over two years due to a largely sedentary lifestyle and progressive deconditioning. He has become increasingly reliant on the installed equipment and support workers. He wants more independence and would like to leave the house more confidently.</p>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:10px;margin:16px 0;"><div style="background:#FEF2F2;border:1px solid #FCA5A5;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);letter-spacing:0.07em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px;">⚠️ Clinical Concern</div><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Equipment installed but problem persists — intervention mismatch</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Physical capacity is the primary driver, not environment</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Progressive deconditioning over 2 years — underaddressed</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Reliance increasing despite supports</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Previous clinicians may have misidentified the driver</li></ul></div><div style="background:#EFF6FF;border:1px solid #BFCBFE;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);letter-spacing:0.07em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px;">🧠 Reasoning Analysis</div><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">PEO: Person domain (capacity/endurance) is primary driver</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Environment was modified — but for the wrong reason</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Equipment may now be enabling avoidance of capacity building</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Capacity building + graded activity likely more impactful</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Behaviour change readiness must be assessed first</li></ul></div><div style="background:var(--gold-pale);border:1px solid #E8C070;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);letter-spacing:0.07em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px;">🎯 Revised Intervention Direction</div><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Capacity building: structured graded activity</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">EP referral for endurance and strength program</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Gradual reduction of dependency on support workers</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Goal: community access and meal independence</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Equipment review — is existing AT still appropriate?</li></ul></div></div>
      <div class="callout gold" style="margin:14px 0 0;"><div class="callout-icon">⚠️</div><div class="callout-content"><strong>Clinician challenge:</strong> Liam says "but the equipment helps me manage." How do you explore whether the equipment is genuinely supportive or enabling further deconditioning?</div></div>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 280px;gap:16px;margin-top:16px;">
      <div style="background:var(--green-xpale);border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:18px 20px;">
        <div style="font-size:10.5px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--green);margin-bottom:12px;">Discussion Questions</div>
        <ol style="padding-left:18px;"><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">Using the PEO model, identify where the primary mismatch is occurring in Liam's situation.</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">What assumption did previous clinicians likely make, and how did this lead to the intervention mismatch?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">Is the current equipment helping Liam — or has it become part of the problem? How would you assess this?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">What would an appropriate new intervention direction look like?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">How do you raise the issue of over-prescription with Liam sensitively?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">When would you trial before prescribing, and when would you act directly?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">How does behaviour change readiness influence your approach to introducing capacity building?</li></ol>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div style="background:var(--navy);border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;margin-bottom:10px;">
          <div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:8px;">Facilitator Focus</div>
          <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:2px;"><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">Over-prescription</span><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">True driver identification</span><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">Capacity vs equipment</span><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">Intervention mismatch</span></div>
        </div>
        <div style="background:var(--gold-pale);border:1px solid #E8C070;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;">
          <div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7A5010;margin-bottom:8px;">💡 Facilitator Insight</div>
          <ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">→ This case is about identifying when environment-focused intervention is the wrong tool.</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">→ Equipment can enable avoidance of capacity building — this must be assessed explicitly.</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">→ Previous clinicians acted in good faith — the learning here is about structured reasoning, not blame.</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">→ Liam's deconditioning is the primary driver: EP referral + graded activity is likely highest-impact.</li></ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    </div>
  </div><div class="takeaways-box"><h3>Key Takeaways</h3><div class="takeaways-grid"><div class="takeaway-item">Clinical reasoning is the foundation of targeted, effective intervention</div><div class="takeaway-item">The reasoning loop — Assess, Interpret, Act, Review — guides structured thinking</div><div class="takeaway-item">Use the PEO model to identify where the mismatch is occurring</div><div class="takeaway-item">Always link reasoning to the participant's readiness for change</div><div class="takeaway-item">Identify the primary driver first — don't address everything at once</div><div class="takeaway-item">Clear decisions (act/trial/refer) reduce unnecessary interventions</div></div></div>
  </div>
</div>

