      <div class="ws-header-left">
        <div class="ws-num-badge">Workshop 05 of 06</div>
        <div class="ws-header-title">Clinical Decision-Making<br>in Core OT Practice Areas</div>
        <div class="ws-header-purpose">Applies clinical reasoning to real-world OT service delivery. Covers selecting pathways (AT, HM, FCA, Capacity Building), structured decision frameworks, SOAP documentation, and aligning interventions with functional outcomes.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="ws-header-right">
        <div class="ws-meta-row"><div class="ws-meta-icon">⏱</div><div><div class="ws-meta-label">Duration</div><div class="ws-meta-val">60 minutes</div></div></div>
        <div class="ws-meta-row"><div class="ws-meta-icon">📋</div><div><div class="ws-meta-label">Sections</div><div class="ws-meta-val">10 Parts + Cases</div></div></div>
        <div class="ws-meta-row"><div class="ws-meta-icon">💡</div><div><div class="ws-meta-label">Focus</div><div class="ws-meta-val">Service Pathways &amp; Documentation</div></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  <div class="objectives-box">
    <h3>Learning Objectives</h3>
    <div class="objectives-grid">
      <div class="obj-item"><div class="obj-dot"></div><span>Select appropriate OT service pathways based on clinical reasoning</span></div>
      <div class="obj-item"><div class="obj-dot"></div><span>Integrate SOAP documentation into clinical thinking</span></div>
      <div class="obj-item"><div class="obj-dot"></div><span>Understand AT, HM, and FCA processes and when each is appropriate</span></div>
      <div class="obj-item"><div class="obj-dot"></div><span>Align interventions with functional outcomes and participant goals</span></div>
      <div class="obj-item"><div class="obj-dot"></div><span>Apply structured decision-making frameworks to service selection</span></div>
      <div class="obj-item"><div class="obj-dot"></div><span>Understand how documentation reflects and supports clinical reasoning</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="timeline-bar" style="margin-bottom:32px;">
    <div class="timeline-seg" style="background:#E4F2EF;"><div class="ts-time" style="color:var(--green);">0-5 min</div><div class="ts-label" style="color:var(--green);">Welcome</div></div>
    <div class="timeline-seg" style="background:#EEF0F4;"><div class="ts-time" style="color:var(--navy);">5-20 min</div><div class="ts-label" style="color:var(--slate);">Parts 1-2: Decision flowchart &amp; services</div></div>
    <div class="timeline-seg" style="background:#EEF0F4;"><div class="ts-time" style="color:var(--navy);">20-32 min</div><div class="ts-label" style="color:var(--slate);">Part 3: SOAP documentation</div></div>
    <div class="timeline-seg" style="background:#FBF3E0;"><div class="ts-time" style="color:#B07820;">32-55 min</div><div class="ts-label" style="color:#7A5010;">Case-based discussion</div></div>
    <div class="timeline-seg" style="background:#E4F2EF;"><div class="ts-time" style="color:var(--green);">55-60 min</div><div class="ts-label" style="color:var(--green);">Takeaways</div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="sec-label"><div class="sec-label-num">1</div><div class="sec-label-text">The OT Decision Flowchart — Problem to Pathway</div><div class="sec-label-bar"></div></div>
  <div class="ot-flow">
    <div class="ot-flow-row"><div class="ot-flow-box problem">🔍 Functional Problem Identified</div></div>
    <div class="ot-flow-row" style="justify-content:center;"><span style="font-size:20px;color:var(--sage);">↓</span></div>
    <div class="ot-flow-row"><div class="ot-flow-box driver">🎯 Identify Primary Driver (use PEO + Driver Hierarchy)</div></div>
    <div class="ot-flow-row" style="justify-content:center;"><span style="font-size:20px;color:var(--sage);">↓</span></div>
    <p style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--slate);text-align:center;margin-bottom:12px;">Select the Most Appropriate Pathway</p>
    <div class="ot-flow-branch"><div class="ot-flow-box at">🦽 Assistive Technology<br><span style="font-size:10px;font-weight:400;">Equipment to support participation</span></div><div class="ot-flow-box hm">🏠 Home Modifications<br><span style="font-size:10px;font-weight:400;">Environmental changes for safety</span></div><div class="ot-flow-box fca">📋 Functional Capacity Assessment<br><span style="font-size:10px;font-weight:400;">Detailed assessment to justify supports</span></div><div class="ot-flow-box cap">💪 Capacity Building<br><span style="font-size:10px;font-weight:400;">Skill development for independence</span></div></div>
    <div class="ot-flow-row" style="justify-content:center;margin-top:12px;"><span style="font-size:20px;color:var(--sage);">↓</span></div>
    <div class="ot-flow-row"><div class="ot-flow-box driver" style="text-align:center;">📄 Document in SOAP Format → Link Problem → Driver → Intervention → Outcome</div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="sec-label"><div class="sec-label-num">2</div><div class="sec-label-text">Service Area Comparison</div><div class="sec-label-bar"></div></div>
  <div class="grid-4">
    <div class="card" style="border-top:3px solid #4F46E5;"><div class="card-title" style="font-size:13px;">🦽 Assistive Technology</div><div class="card-body" style="font-size:12px;"><ul><li>Equipment supports participation</li><li>Independence can be gained with aids</li><li>Trial before formal prescription</li></ul></div></div>
    <div class="card" style="border-top:3px solid #D97706;"><div class="card-title" style="font-size:13px;">🏠 Home Modifications</div><div class="card-body" style="font-size:12px;"><ul><li>Environmental barriers are the primary driver</li><li>Safety risk is present</li><li>Long-term access improvement needed</li></ul></div></div>
    <div class="card" style="border-top:3px solid #059669;"><div class="card-title" style="font-size:13px;">📋 FCA</div><div class="card-body" style="font-size:12px;"><ul><li>NDIS support justification needed</li><li>Complex functional picture</li><li>Must link findings to function</li></ul></div></div>
    <div class="card" style="border-top:3px solid #BE185D;"><div class="card-title" style="font-size:13px;">💪 Capacity Building</div><div class="card-body" style="font-size:12px;"><ul><li>Participant has potential to build skills</li><li>Confidence or routine is the main barrier</li><li>Long-term independence is the goal</li></ul></div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="sec-label"><div class="sec-label-num">3</div><div class="sec-label-text">SOAP Note Documentation</div><div class="sec-label-bar"></div></div>
  <div class="soap-flow">
    <div class="soap-card"><div class="soap-header" style="background:var(--green);"><div class="soap-letter">S</div><div class="soap-word">SUBJECTIVE</div></div><div class="soap-body"><p>What the participant reports</p><div class="soap-example">"Reports increased fatigue when cooking — needs to rest after 5 minutes."</div></div></div>
    <div class="soap-card"><div class="soap-header" style="background:#3B82F6;"><div class="soap-letter">O</div><div class="soap-word">OBJECTIVE</div></div><div class="soap-body"><p>What you clinically observe</p><div class="soap-example">Required rest breaks after 5 min standing. Reduced grip strength bilaterally.</div></div></div>
    <div class="soap-card"><div class="soap-header" style="background:#F59E0B;"><div class="soap-letter">A</div><div class="soap-word">ASSESSMENT</div></div><div class="soap-body"><p>Your clinical interpretation</p><div class="soap-example">Fatigue + reduced grip is limiting meal preparation and independence at home.</div></div></div>
    <div class="soap-card"><div class="soap-header" style="background:#8B5CF6;"><div class="soap-letter">P</div><div class="soap-word">PLAN</div></div><div class="soap-body"><p>Next steps — linked to findings</p><div class="soap-example">Trial seated meal prep + energy conservation strategies. Review in 2 sessions.</div></div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="callout teal" style="margin-top:14px;"><div class="callout-icon">📄</div><div class="callout-content"><strong>Documentation should clearly link:</strong> what is happening → why it matters → what will be done next.</div></div>
  <div class="sec-label"><div class="sec-label-num">4</div><div class="sec-label-text">Case-Based Discussion</div><div class="sec-label-bar"></div></div>
  <div class="case-card" style="margin-bottom:24px;">
    <div class="case-header"><div class="case-badge">Case 1</div><div class="case-title">Rebecca — "Equipment That Will Make Everything Easier"</div></div>
    <div class="case-body">
      <div style="margin-bottom:12px;"><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;background:var(--green-pale);color:var(--green);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:600;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:12px;margin:2px 3px 2px 0;">Age: <span style="font-weight:400;">48</span></span><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;background:var(--green-pale);color:var(--green);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:600;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:12px;margin:2px 3px 2px 0;">Diagnosis: <span style="font-weight:400;">Multiple sclerosis</span></span><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;background:var(--green-pale);color:var(--green);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:600;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:12px;margin:2px 3px 2px 0;">Workshop Focus: <span style="font-weight:400;">AT vs capacity building</span></span></div>
      <p class="case-scenario">Rebecca is a 48-year-old woman with MS experiencing fatigue, reduced grip, and poor task tolerance. She requests "equipment that will make everything easier." On assessment, she has become increasingly inactive over 18 months, is reliant on support workers for tasks she previously completed independently, and avoids tasks she can still technically perform. There is clinical concern that introducing more equipment may increase dependency. Her NDIS plan review is in three months.</p>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:10px;margin:16px 0;"><div style="background:#FEF2F2;border:1px solid #FCA5A5;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);letter-spacing:0.07em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px;">⚠️ Clinical Risk</div><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">AT request without capacity assessment</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Increasing inactivity + reliance 18 months</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Avoidance of tasks she can technically do</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">AT may reinforce dependency</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">NDIS review pressure — risk of rushed recommendation</li></ul></div><div style="background:#EFF6FF;border:1px solid #BFCBFE;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);letter-spacing:0.07em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px;">🔄 Intervention Decision</div><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Primary driver: deconditioning + avoidance</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Capacity building first: graded task reintroduction</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Trial: what can Rebecca do with minimal adaptation?</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">EP referral: fatigue management + endurance</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">AT for genuinely limiting deficits only</li></ul></div><div style="background:var(--gold-pale);border:1px solid #E8C070;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);letter-spacing:0.07em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px;">🎯 Pathway</div><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Trial tasks before prescribing equipment</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Support worker role: coach not carer where possible</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">FCA may be needed for NDIS review</li></ul></div></div>
      
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 280px;gap:16px;margin-top:16px;">
      <div style="background:var(--green-xpale);border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:18px 20px;">
        <div style="font-size:10.5px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--green);margin-bottom:12px;">Discussion Questions</div>
        <ol style="padding-left:18px;"><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">What is the primary driver of Rebecca's difficulty?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">What are the risks of immediately prescribing AT?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">Which pathway(s) would you select and in what sequence?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">How would you structure a trial approach?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">How would you explain to Rebecca why you are not immediately providing equipment?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">What documentation is needed for her NDIS review?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">When does support worker involvement become a barrier rather than support?</li></ol>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div style="background:var(--navy);border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;margin-bottom:10px;">
          <div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:8px;">Facilitator Focus</div>
          <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:2px;"><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">AT vs capacity building</span><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">Dependency risk</span><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">Trialling</span><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">NDIS documentation</span></div>
        </div>
        <div style="background:var(--gold-pale);border:1px solid #E8C070;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;">
          <div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7A5010;margin-bottom:8px;">💡 Facilitator Insight</div>
          <ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">→ Prescribing AT when capacity building is the primary need can accelerate dependency.</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">→ Trial first: what can Rebecca do with modified technique before equipment is considered?</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">→ Support workers operating as carers rather than coaches may be a significant part of the problem.</li></ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    </div>
  </div><div class="case-card" style="margin-bottom:24px;">
    <div class="case-header"><div class="case-badge">Case 2</div><div class="case-title">Mark — "The Complex FCA Under Pressure"</div></div>
    <div class="case-body">
      <div style="margin-bottom:12px;"><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;background:var(--green-pale);color:var(--green);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:600;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:12px;margin:2px 3px 2px 0;">Age: <span style="font-weight:400;">28</span></span><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;background:var(--green-pale);color:var(--green);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:600;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:12px;margin:2px 3px 2px 0;">Diagnosis: <span style="font-weight:400;">Acquired brain injury · Executive dysfunction</span></span><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;background:var(--green-pale);color:var(--green);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:600;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:12px;margin:2px 3px 2px 0;">Workshop Focus: <span style="font-weight:400;">FCA complexity · Documentation</span></span></div>
      <p class="case-scenario">Mark is a 28-year-old with ABI resulting in executive dysfunction and emotional dysregulation. He struggles with employment, daily routines, budgeting, and consistent self-care. His functional presentation varies significantly day-to-day. His parents advocate strongly for increased NDIS funding and pressure the OT to complete the FCA quickly with clear recommendations. There is a genuine funding need — but conclusions drawn too quickly risk misrepresenting his actual functional capacity.</p>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:10px;margin:16px 0;"><div style="background:#FEF2F2;border:1px solid #FCA5A5;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);letter-spacing:0.07em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px;">⚠️ Assessment Complexity</div><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Significant day-to-day variability</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Executive dysfunction: task initiation inconsistent</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Parents advocating for outcome rather than process</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Risk of rushed conclusions → inaccurate report</li></ul></div><div style="background:#EFF6FF;border:1px solid #BFCBFE;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);letter-spacing:0.07em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px;">🧠 Clinical Reasoning Needs</div><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Multiple assessment points needed</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Structured observations across different contexts</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Distinguish genuine deficit from variability</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Carer report vs independent function discrepancy</li></ul></div><div style="background:var(--gold-pale);border:1px solid #E8C070;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;"><div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);letter-spacing:0.07em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px;">📄 Documentation Standards</div><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">SOAP notes must reflect variability explicitly</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">Justify supports with functional evidence, not diagnosis alone</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">FCA report: what is happening → why → what is needed</li></ul></div></div>
      
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 280px;gap:16px;margin-top:16px;">
      <div style="background:var(--green-xpale);border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:18px 20px;">
        <div style="font-size:10.5px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--green);margin-bottom:12px;">Discussion Questions</div>
        <ol style="padding-left:18px;"><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">What areas should the FCA assess for Mark, and why is a single-session assessment insufficient?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">How does Mark's day-to-day variability affect the assessment process?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">How should the OT manage the pressure from Mark's parents?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">What risks exist if the OT rushes the assessment?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">How would you structure SOAP documentation across multiple sessions?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">What is the difference between a diagnosis-justified and function-justified support recommendation?</li><li style="padding:5px 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--body);line-height:1.55;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.05);">At what point does the OT have an obligation to push back on a family-imposed timeline?</li></ol>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div style="background:var(--navy);border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;margin-bottom:10px;">
          <div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:8px;">Facilitator Focus</div>
          <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:2px;"><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">Assessment complexity</span><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">Fluctuating presentation</span><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">Documentation quality</span><span style="background:var(--navy);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-size:10.5px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin:2px;">Clinical integrity</span></div>
        </div>
        <div style="background:var(--gold-pale);border:1px solid #E8C070;border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:14px;">
          <div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7A5010;margin-bottom:8px;">💡 Facilitator Insight</div>
          <ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;"><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">→ Diagnosis alone does not justify supports — functional impact must be clearly documented.</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">→ Rushing an FCA risks either over- or under-justifying Mark's needs.</li><li style="padding:2px 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--body);">→ Multiple observation points across contexts is best practice for ABI.</li></ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    </div>
  </div><div class="takeaways-box"><h3>Key Takeaways</h3><div class="takeaways-grid"><div class="takeaway-item">Intervention selection should be guided by clinical reasoning, not habit or client request alone</div><div class="takeaway-item">Documentation reflects and supports clinical reasoning — not just administrative compliance</div><div class="takeaway-item">AT, HM, FCA and capacity building each serve distinct purposes</div><div class="takeaway-item">Interventions should always align with meaningful participant outcomes</div><div class="takeaway-item">Identifying the primary driver is critical for effective service selection</div><div class="takeaway-item">Clear decision-making improves efficiency, consistency and quality of care</div></div></div>
  </div>
</div>

